                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239228888",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197991040157",
                            "num_reviews": 12,
                            "playtime_forever": 339,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 339,
                            "deck_playtime_at_review": 339,
                            "last_played": 1746064516
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The extent to which you enjoy Kentucky Route Zero depends entirely on your level of patience. Initially, your introduced to a beautiful, lonely, and dreamlike game - clearly a meditation but with themes yet to be revealed. \n\nAs time goes on you will realize that a key theme is lack of agency - being trapped in debt, in poverty, by circumstance. Interesting themes, but ones that for me translated into: lack of gameplay. \n\nUltimately KRZ becomes a game about walking to places and talking to people. If you're into that, be my guest and try the game. But I have a limited amount of time to play games, and once you see though the facade this media is a multi act play that pretends to be a game. A chosen-for-you Adventure. And whatever my affinity is for the story, the accumulated time spent moving between people and selecting choices became too high a price for the ticket. \n\nIf you're like me, pour a glass of Hard Times Whiskey and just watch a playthrough.",
